# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD is `/usr/local/sbin/hs-start.sh`, which backgrounds
# sshd, mariadb (bound to 0.0.0.0:3306), httpd (ServerTokens Full +
# /server-status), vsftpd (anon), xinetd/telnet (:23), crond and the planted
# ncat listener, then `wait`s. So every seeded misconfiguration is LIVE at
# first boot, which is what makes verify.sh's behavioural probes (curl
# /server-status, ss :3306, ftp anon, telnet :23, nc :$listener_port)
# meaningful.
#
# PID 1 is hs-start.sh (a `wait` over all daemons), NOT any single service,
# so a solution may restart httpd/mariadb without killing the container.
#
# Without this marker the harness overrides CMD with `sleep infinity`: no
# daemon boots, every service check fails (-10 each) and the service-dependent
# non-service checks become meaningless (false-pass).
